note as pgboss_note
PGBoss Job Queue Schema
====
Separate "pgboss" schema contains:
- Job queue tables (auto-managed)
- Background processing system
- AI analysis and embedding generation
- Scheduling and retry logic
- Operational isolation from main schema
end note

note as architecture_note
Key Architectural Features (Post-Rebase)
====
• Entity Graph System: Unified entities with typed relationships
• Digital Footprint Tracking: Real-time activity monitoring
• Communication Intelligence: Sentiment analysis and embeddings
• Device Management: IoT sensors with PostGIS support  
• Multi-Modal Embeddings: Visual, textual, and semantic vectors
• Privacy Controls: Granular privacy settings and sensitive content detection
• TimescaleDB Optimization: Multiple hypertables for different data types
• Legacy Migration: Gradual transition from old schema
• Background Processing: Distributed AI analysis via PGBoss
end note

note as migration_note
Schema Evolution
====
Major Changes in Rebase:
• Removed: people, contacts, places, locations, things, embeddings tables
• Added: Entity graph system (entities, relationships, communications)
• Added: Digital footprint tracking (browser_activity, screen_captures)  
• Added: Device management (devices, sensors)
• Enhanced: Actions with priority field
• Restructured: Message-file relationships (message_files table)
• Migration: Legacy tables marked for gradual transition
end note

@enduml